── Runtime dependency ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

NumPy                        BSD-3-Clause
    The sole runtime dependency. The synthesis core is a sequence of
    singular value decompositions, so there is no honest way to avoid it;
    see the "one dependency" note in the README.


── Optional dependencies (plotting, dev tooling, cross-validation) ──────

matplotlib                  BSD-style (Matplotlib License)
    Optional; only used by TradeoffProfile.plot() and the --plot CLI flag.
SciPy                        BSD-3-Clause
    Dev/test only; used to independently verify circuit constructions
    against scipy.linalg.expm in tests/test_decompose.py.
pytest                       MIT
mypy                         MIT
ruff                         MIT
Qiskit                       Apache-2.0
    Dev/test only. Used two ways: (1) as an export target
    (mpsynth.exporters.to_qiskit / build_qiskit), and (2) as the
    independent baseline in validation/run_validation.py -- its own
    Statevector simulator and StatePreparation construction are what
    MPSynth's fidelity and CNOT-count claims are cross-validated against,
    deliberately not using MPSynth's own code to check MPSynth's own
    arithmetic.
qiskit-qasm3-import           Apache-2.0
    Dev/test only; round-trips exported OpenQASM 3.0 back through
    Qiskit's own parser in tests/test_exporters.py.
PennyLane                    Apache-2.0
    Optional export target and dev/test dependency; used to verify the
    big-endian amplitude-order convention independently of Qiskit's
    little-endian one.

Exact pinned version floors are in pyproject.toml. Where a licence is
stated above it reflects each project's own declaration at the time of
writing; consult each project for authoritative terms.


── Frameworks targeted by the exporters (not runtime dependencies) ─────

OpenQASM 2.0 / 3.0, QIR (LLVM base profile) and Q# are text/IR formats
MPSynth emits; no code from any of their reference implementations is
vendored or redistributed here.


── Standards and specifications ─────────────────────────────────────────

OpenQASM 2.0 / 3.0 and the QIR specification define the two textual
formats mpsynth.exporters.qasm and mpsynth.exporters.qir emit. The
implementations here are original; the specifications are their
respective standards bodies'.
